[h1]OpenZone Storage[/h1]
Virtual storage boxes for the OpenZone series: a box whose contents do not exist in the game world while it is closed, so the loot of a closed box is not in the world at all.

[b]What you get[/b]
[list]
[*]Three boxes from three kits: Small (250 cells, 2 weapon slots, a wooden crate), Medium (500 cells, 4 slots, a sea chest) and Large (1000 cells, 6 slots, a sea chest). A kit is deployed from the hands: pick the spot, turn the hologram with the wheel, hold the action for ten seconds.
[*]One verb on the box, "Look in the box". The placed box is only the anchor: its contents are read from the bridge's database, streamed to your screen, and every drag is one operation the server performs and writes before the next. The session ends when the last player looking closes the screen, walks off, leaves or dies; nothing is on a timer.
[*]Across the box's edge the inventory works the vanilla way: stacks merge when dragged onto each other (from a pocket or off the ground, both ways), a loose item dropped on a box item changes places with it, and [b]Alt+click[/b] moves an item between the box and your inventory or hands.
[*]A search bar that shades what does not match (a container stays lit if a match is inside, however deep), a Sort button, and a Count button (in total and by class).
[*][b]The personal stash.[/b] An admin places a locker, a placed item saved with the world. A player presses F on it and is shown a record of their own, keyed by which locker and whose: one locker holds one stash per player. It carries the character's own thirteen slots and four weapon slots, so a whole kit hangs up instead of being piled into a grid, and clothing hung there keeps working pockets. Nothing stands in the world for it: the record goes to that one player's screen only, and the pairing of locker and player is made on the server from who sent the message.
[*]An admin web page served by the bridge: box lists, contents, history and rollback, and three live commands to the running game; signing in through Discord is optional.
[/list]
[b]Requires[/b] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1559212036]Community Framework[/url], [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3798432022]OpenZone Core[/url], and the OpenZone bridge [b]0.5.0 or newer[/b] running on the server ([url=https://github.com/OpenZone-DayZ/openzone-bridge]github.com/OpenZone-DayZ/openzone-bridge[/url]).
[b]For server owners[/b] The kits are not in the shipped economy: an example types.xml lists all six classes at nominal 0, so you decide how kits reach players.
[b]Source code[/b] [url=https://github.com/OpenZone-DayZ/openzone-storage]github.com/OpenZone-DayZ/openzone-storage[/url]

[b]Licence, repacking, selling[/b]
You may repack this mod into your server's own pack, keeping the attribution and the same licence. You may not sell it, sublicense it or include it in any paid bundle. Running it on a server that accepts donations, sells cosmetics or priority queue slots is fine. CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with the additional permission in NOTICE.

